📱 Mobile-Friendly Features — Complete Checklist
 
✅ Core Layout & Responsiveness
 
- Fluid, percentage-based widths — no fixed pixel widths; use  max-width  containers
- Responsive breakpoints: 360px (small phones), 480px, 768px (tablets), 1024px+
- Viewport meta tag:  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no"> 
- Box-sizing: border-box so padding doesn’t break widths
- Vertical flow first — single column on phones; multi-column only on larger screens
 
👆 Touch & Interaction
 
- Minimum touch target size: 48×48px for buttons/links; ≥8px spacing between them
- Large interactive elements — avoid tiny links/buttons
- Simplified navigation: hamburger menu, bottom tab bar, or slide-out panel
- Swipe gestures — for galleries, carousels, navigating between screens
- No hover-only actions — hover doesn't work reliably on touch; make actions tap-friendly
- Prevent accidental taps — enough spacing between close buttons/links
 
⚡ Performance
 
- Responsive images:  srcset  +  sizes , serve WebP/AVIF; lazy load offscreen images
- Minimize text input — use dropdowns, radio buttons, date pickers instead
- Keep forms short — split long forms across multiple steps
- Fast load: aim for <2s; compress assets; minify CSS/JS; use CDN
- Avoid heavy animations — prefer  transform / opacity  for smooth GPU-accelerated motion
 
📝 Readability & Content
 
- Font size ≥14px on small screens; line-height 1.4–1.6
- Good contrast ratio — at least 4.5:1 for text
- Short paragraphs — 2–3 sentences max; use bullet points
- Clear hierarchy — H1 → H2 → H3; avoid deep nesting
- Don’t shrink text to fit — let it wrap naturally
 
🧠 Smart Mobile Behaviors
 
- Auto-zoom prevention on form focus
- Appropriate input types:  type="tel"  for phones,  type="email" ,  type="number" 
- Numeric keyboard for PIN/currency inputs
- Disable text select/copy only when truly needed
- Pull-to-refresh option for dynamic content
- Infinite scroll or "Load More" pagination
- Sticky headers/footers — keep nav visible while scrolling
 
